// Combat AI profiles, read by the Fenia combat AI (dreamland_fenia/utils/combat ai).
// Profile names: a-z, 0-9, _ only. Field reference: header of "utils/combat ai"
// and "utils/combat ai: moves". Texts are RU; EN/UA via the catalog, section
// "utils/combat ai". Integers only (Fenia has no floats).
// tier_normal (tiers 6-8) and tier_trash (9) drive spells only, melee stays
// with the random pick in global/onFightAI/ai_basic (no blunders: those are
// melee-round slips).
// tier_elite/tier_champion/tier_boss: templates the tier AI fills with each
// mob's own toolbox (.tmp.cai.tierProfile). tier_champion/_boss/_legend have
// phases [{hp, beats, rage, blunder, priority}]: phase i opens below its hp
// (boss/legend 100-60-30, champion 100-30), beats = % change of the lag the
// mob's own skills leave (-100 = none), rage = the damroll boost; drSecs = one
// knockdown/stun and one disarm per target per that many seconds. boss_scenes: lines played when a
// phase opens, by mob vnum, else generic.<template>; keys are phase indexes.
// tier_spells: spell groups by class act; spell_damtypes: spell -> .tables.damage_table name (Fenia cannot read
// it from the spell); spell_prayers: prayer-only spells; spell_rules: who a
// spell can hurt (vict) and who can cast it usefully (caster).
// spell_tiers: attack spell -> damage tier from its skill XML <tier>;
// spell_tier_weight[tier]: % of a tier-3 nuke's damage at L75, so the tier
// AI casts the strongest first. tier_spells debuffs: what each class can cast.
// debuff_rules (move debuff): target role pet (NPC caster on the players'
// side) / caster (player with the caster flag) / melee. lead[class] goes first
// on any player; first[role] = groups tried in order, a random pick inside a
// group, "silence" = the mob's silence spell (silence: evil sentient caster ->
// garble, else by class). Then regen (target has regeneration), agile (agile
// class), then the rest at random. never[role] is never cast; randomPct = %
// of casts that skip the order. glows: affects a "glowing" dispel goes after
// (players only, not permanent ones). No per-target cap for champion+.
// tier_spells ranged: {spell, chance} tried in order at a foe a few rooms
// away (utils/mob brain castRanged); the first that passes its roll casts.
// Champion+ end with strikes (one more blow on a round no move fired); boss
// and legend try rend (tear off the target's sanctuary after a tool landed).
// leash: rooms from home a champion+ chases its last foe (utils/mob brain);
// evadeSecs: seconds with no reachable foe before it gives up, heals and
// goes home. An elite has evadeSecs and no leash: it never chases, but one
// sniped from where it cannot walk gives up the same way.
// extraStrikes: plain blows a boss/legend adds every tier round; crushPct: % of
// rounds a melee-only one (no spells, no breath, not blinded) lands a blow past
// shield, parry and dodge (dice + damroll x1.5, red line). Service NPCs neither.
